A||||12||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||Bought New Car:  Contour SVT in my driveway!||||1||
Z||000000||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||07-03-2001||11:53 PM||||Hi,<P>I have three Fieros.  I love them dearly, but . . .<P>We just bought a 2000 SVT Ford Contour and it is hard to even think of words to describe it.<P>The car is black with black leather, power everything, tilt/slide sunroof, 200 HP SVT 2.5L V6, ABS, dual exhaust with chrome tips, 5 spd, CD, keyless entry with alarm, etc.  The list is endless.  The car even came with a K&N open element air filter, factory stock!<P>It has only 7000 miles on it.  It still smells like new.  The sound of that engine is enough to make a grown man cry.  <P>I may be a proponent of the Iron Duke, but there is nothing like an SVT V6 when it comes to sounding bad ass while still very quiet.  The car is stable on all roads and the seats are totally supportive yet sooooo comfy all the time. <P>I will post pictures tomorrow when the sun is out.  If you have never seen an SVT Contour (like me about 5 hours ago), you will be very surprised by it.<P>As my wife said earlier "It hangs corners like a Fiero . . ."<P>Enough said.  <P>Thanks for the opportunity to vent all of that enthusiasm.  I have never owned a new bichin' car like this one.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-04-2001||12:20 AM||||I drove a few of those when i workeda t the car dealership. Personally I'm not a fan of any Ford product. But I do have to say if i was going to go with one, I'd probably go with that. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||07-04-2001||10:09 AM||||Those SVT Contours are sweet! Couple of years ago, my dad seriously considered buying one. He decided he wanted to lease, and the every local Ford dealersahip wanted $500/month for a lease, because they considered the car a "collectors item" or something. He told them he could buy a 'vette for less than that, and said forget it. <P>I'll never forget how well that car handled, or how that 6 sounded. He almost got the all black with black leather too. As I recall, the only option on the SVT Contour is the sunroof. Every other "option" is standard. Isn't 2000 the last model year for them? Too bad they are gone, they look good.||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||07-04-2001||10:33 AM||||    They were probobly kicking themselves....They couldn't give those things away at most dealerships. By the end of the model year most dealerships were cutting half the price tag. Not my favorite car but at least it's not one of those svt focus's. Can somebody please explain to me the purpose of that!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000004||DecadenceR||07-04-2001||12:11 PM||||The SVT Focus is trying to me the american equivalent of all the rice burners. I've seen all kinds of kits and ****  for them already too.||||reg||1
Z||000005||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||07-04-2001||05:34 PM||||I am having my first problem with the 2000 Contour SVT.<P>My wife and the car have vanished.  They left before I got up this morning and I don't know where they went.  It's been about 5 hours since I got up and the driveway is empty.  <P>A day ago, she was not a car enthusiast.  Now, I think she is out getting even with everybody that passed her in our 1994 Ford Ranger 4 cylinder.  Dr. Jeckyl/Mr. Hyde?<P>I was going to post pictures, but I guess that will have to wait until the car comes back.  I hope it does soon, I want to drive it!||||reg||12
Z||000006||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||07-04-2001||06:06 PM||||Mwahaha.<P>- Da Wife||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||07-04-2001||08:05 PM||||IWANT! <BR>IWANT!<BR>IWANT!<P>If Ford still made those things, I probably would have already bought one. We have an X-Plan deal through our company, but I just haven't found any other Ford that stirs my soul.<P>Having said that...<BR>I understand that Ford pretty much treats the SVT Contour the same way GM treats the Fiero. Completely ignores them. <P>Congrats on your find, and good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
